###################################################################################################
#                                                                                    3.6.0-Cordelia
#
#     At a Lunar Eclipse                               .oooooo.             ooooo   ooooo        
#     ==================                              d8P    Y8b             888     888         
# Thy shadow, Earth, from Pole to Central Sea,       888           .ooooo.   888     888         
# Now steals along upon the Moon's meek shine        888          d88   88b  888ooooo888         
# In even monochrome and curving line                888          888   888  888     888  dP^Y8b 
# Of imperturbable serenity.                          88b    ooo  888   888  888     888      8P 
#                                                      Y8bood8P    Y8bod8P' o888o   o888o   <8B  
# How shall I link such sun-cast symmetry                                               8b    8b 
# With the torn troubled form I know as thine,                                           Y8oo8P  
# That profile, placid as a brow divine,
# With continents of moil and misery?
#
# And can immense Mortality but throw                  Is such the stellar gauge of earthly show,
# So small a shade, and Heaven's high human scheme   Nation at war with nation, brains that teem,
# Be hemmed within the coasts yon arc implies?           Heroes, and women fairer than the skies?
#
#                                                                                    Thomas Hardy
#
